---
// VRF explainer section -- how commit-reveal works, technical but accessible
---

<section id="how-it-works" class="py-24 px-6 border-t border-stone-800">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-amber-400 mb-4">How It Works</h2>
    <p class="text-amber-400/50 mb-12 text-lg">
      Commit-reveal via on-chain VRF. No server involved in outcome derivation.
    </p>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      <!-- Step 1 -->
      <div class="border border-stone-800 rounded-lg p-6">
        <div class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-2xl font-bold mb-3">01</div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400/90 mb-2">Commit</h3>
        <p class="text-amber-400/50 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Your flip() transaction commits to VRF beacon round N+8 (~22 seconds ahead).
          Your salt hash is stored on-chain -- the house cannot predict or influence the outcome.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 2 -->
      <div class="border border-stone-800 rounded-lg p-6">
        <div class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-2xl font-bold mb-3">02</div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400/90 mb-2">VRF Beacon</h3>
        <p class="text-amber-400/50 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Applied Blockchain's beacon (app ID 947957720) publishes a VRF output for round N+8.
          This output is tamper-proof and unpredictable before the round occurs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 3 -->
      <div class="border border-stone-800 rounded-lg p-6">
        <div class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-2xl font-bold mb-3">03</div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400/90 mb-2">Resolve</h3>
        <p class="text-amber-400/50 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          resolve() reads the beacon output via inner app call.
          outcome = SHA-256(beacon_output ++ your_salt_hash)[0] % 2.
          If you win, HouseTreasury pays out instantly on-chain.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Code snippet -->
    <div class="mt-12 bg-stone-900 border border-stone-800 rounded-lg p-6 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto">
      <p class="text-amber-400/40 mb-4">// On-chain outcome derivation (AVM, Puya Python)</p>
      <pre class="text-amber-400/80 leading-relaxed"><code>randomness = arc4.abi_call("must_get(uint64,byte[])byte[]", commit_round)
beacon_output = randomness.bytes[2:]  # skip ARC-4 length prefix
combined = beacon_output + salt_hash
outcome = sha256(combined)[0] % 2     # 0=tails 1=heads</code></pre>
    </div>

    <!-- Proof card link -->
    <div class="mt-8 text-center">
      <p class="text-amber-400/40 text-sm">
        Every flip generates a shareable VRF proof card PNG --
        <a href="https://app.fairground.xyz" class="text-amber-400 underline underline-offset-2">play to get yours</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
